<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/14th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Great Troubles</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1359">1359</a>–<a href="/years/1381">1381</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Great Turmoil</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Great Troubles were a period of civil war in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-horde">Golden Horde</a> from 1359 to 1381, after the murder of Khan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berdibeg">Berdi Beg</a>. Over twenty khans rose and fell, while the warlord <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamai">Mamai</a> ruled the west through puppet khans. The chaos loosened the Horde's grip on the Rus' principalities, letting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> defeat Mamai at Kulikovo in 1380, before <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokhtamysh">Tokhtamysh</a> reunited the khanate.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/great-troubles.jpg" alt="Great Troubles" width="159" height="181" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tibicena · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mamai.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
